    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "auto-docs — the index is generated, the meaning is authored",
      "prov:value": "> in cat-harness needs to be harness/handler at\n> `cat-harness/auto-docs/<auto-doc-type>/<path>` defined. which will\n> auto-generate extracatable documentation at `<path>` sub-graph."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The obligation: reference the index, then say what it cannot",
      "prov:value": "**An index with no authored prose around it reads as complete while explaining\nnothing.** That is the `xom7` shape — *it looks exactly like a working one from\nin here* — moved into documentation, and it is the failure this skill is\nwritten against."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reuse the assets; never restate them",
      "prov:value": "> *\"..reuse assets in explain.\"*"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the handler emits, and what it does not",
      "prov:value": "**Read the type list off `TYPES` in `gen-auto-docs.ts`, not off this table.**\nThe table below was wrong on two rows until 2026-09-24 — it called `glossary`\nunbuilt while it was emitting pages, and omitted `index/docs` entirely — which\nis the failure this skill's own §Related points at `uses-editorial-review` for.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the handler emits, and what it does not",
      "prov:value": "**`glossary` moved rows, and `lqo9` has not been told.** It was listed here as\n*\"gated by bean `lqo9`'s roast\"*. That roast was held on 2026-09-20 and the\ntype now builds — `auto-docs/glossary/` carries an `index.html` and a\n`glossary/` subtree. Bean `lqo9` is still open and still carries the gating as\na live constraint on its own remaining work, so a reader arriving from either\nside is told the glossary index is blocked on something that has been\novertaken. Whoever next works `lqo9` should re-scope it against what is\nactually emitting.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean lqo9",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the handler emits, and what it does not",
      "prov:value": "**`toc` is out and stays out.** Owner: *\"no toc,... ther is no meanging at\nfolio level/. (mayber later)\"* — a table of contents is a document-order\nnotion and a sub-graph has no single order to take one over."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two rules the generator keeps, and why they are not incidental",
      "prov:value": "**A type names the GRAPH TYPOLOGY its artefacts live in.** The first draft walked\nevery declared directory and reported **1,522** skills where `knownSkills()`\nfinds 219 — `docs/` is declared too, and holds a generated markdown rendering\nof every skill, so each was counted again as a second skill. *A rendering of an\nartefact is not the artefact.*"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two rules the generator keeps, and why they are not incidental",
      "prov:value": "**Ask the repository's own function; do not re-derive its rule.** The second\ndraft walked the skill directories recursively and reported 227 against 219.\nAll seven extras were `skills/<package>/<skill>/<page>.md` — supporting pages\n*inside* a skill, which carry the same front matter and are not skills.\n`skillMdDirs()` already encodes that distinction, so the generator calls it.\nTwo answers to \"what is a skill\" is one answer too many."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The sub-graph segment is the declared `id`, not its path",
      "prov:value": "The owner wrote `<path>`; the URL carries the declared entry's **`id`**.\nDeliberate, and the reasons are `state-visualizer`'s own: `id` is what\n`<name>.json` declares and what an override matches on, so an id-derived URL\n**survives the directory moving**. It also stays one segment, which is what\nlets `orphanSubjectPages()` prune with an exact ownership test rather than a\nfourth pruner (bean `ankg` asks for no more of those). Each page **states its\ndeclared path**, so nothing is lost — the mapping lives on the artefact rather\nthan only in the URL.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ankg"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "An empty sub-graph gets no page",
      "prov:value": "A sub-graph contributing nothing to a type is not rendered. A declared-but-\nempty directory with a page claiming to index it is the `dh4f` defect as a nav\nentry: a link that resolves to nothing while reading as a section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/auto-docs.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Related",
      "prov:value": "- [`readme-sections`](readme-sections.md) — the same split one level out: the\n  platform owns the markers, the folio owns the file.\n- [`uses-editorial-review`](../../authoring/authoring-core/uses-editorial-review.md) — why a count in prose is\n  a claim rather than evidence, which is why these pages compute their counts.\n- Bean `06e3` — the handler, the authoring rule, the per-harness docs landing\n  page and its QA check, and the navbar over harnesses with populated `docs/`.\n  **Their states differ and are worth naming separately**, because this entry\n  said \"the last two are not built\" until 2026-09-24 and one of them was\n  gating CI at the time:\n  - the **QA check** is **built and gated** — `check:docs-populated`\n    (`package.json`, run by `code-quality-gates.yml`);\n  - the **landing page** is **not built**. `06e3` records one at\n    `cat-harness/docs/cat-harness/index.md`; there is no such file, and\n    `<base>/cat-harness/` is served by `published-graphs.md`, which is\n    GENERATED. So §\"The obligation\" above is **unmet** for that route rather\n    than satisfied — an index with no authored prose around it is exactly what\n    this skill exists to refuse;\n  - the **navbar** is **not built**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 06e3",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
